  "implemented": [
    "Actual AgentManager retains its sessions.size aggregate, including idle/coordinator sessions. Synchronous local intent tickets do not claim an applied native grant; Source reconciles one captured optional native callback without UI/window lifetime dependence.",
    "Existing exact private host.sleep.set boolean DTO reports applied state. True requires captured host capability and current Source scope; false retains cleanup authority after acquisition scope loss. No new public commands, cookies, paths, flags or renderer grants.",
    "Source serializes raw activation/release, coalesces tickets, never blindly retries uncertain activation and keeps durable sessions running on optional denial. Late activation is released; failed cleanup retains ownership and blocks profile release until an explicit cleanup retry succeeds.",
    "Linux opens a private GIO bus connection with an unpredictable token, captures the unique portal owner, subscribes before Inhibit and requires both the exact returned object-path handle and Response0 before reporting true. Fixed suspend-only flag4, fixed reason, empty parent and bounded exact GVariant decoding.",
    "Scope loss, portal/connection loss, cancellation and pending deadlines retire the privately owned connection. Retained callbacks, signals and timer retire before cleanup acknowledgement; failed close retains ownership for retry. Private disconnect cleanup follows the reviewed portal1.20.4 request lifecycle.",
    "Application shutdown cancels native energy before draining ordinary work, so an unanswered portal interaction cannot block its own cancellation. Source host drain independently closes energy before profile release.",
    "No dependency, manifest, package/runtime pin, database schema or public command/event surface changes."
  ],
